"line":548,"character":4},"end":{"line":553,"character":5}},"parameters":[]},{"yarnName":"movement","definitionName":"global::DialogueManager.Movement","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","documentation":"Triggers a named scripted move from a Cutscener in the scene \u2014 e.g. <<movement JoshHome>> walks whatever object/destination pair was named \"JoshHome\" in that Cutscener's Inspector list. Optional modifier words, in any order: freeze \u2014 the dialogue waits until the move actually finishes before showing the next line. Without it, the line advances immediately and the move plays out in the background. hold   \u2014 the sprite KEEPS the facing it already had for the whole move, instead of turning to follow the direction of travel. Use it with a <<face>> right before, when a character has to walk while still looking at someone: floating backwards, backing away, being pulled. flip   \u2014 invert the sprite once before setting off, then hold that. Legacy: it's a guess about which way the art currently points, so <<face>> plus hold is the version that's actually right every time. e.g. <<movement JoshHome freeze>>, <<movement HazeFloatDown hold freeze>>.","language":"csharp","async":true,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":569,"character":4},"end":{"line":592,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"movementName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"},{"name":"modifier1","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"},{"name":"modifier2","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"},{"name":"modifier3","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"enable","definitionName":"global::DialogueManager.Enable","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","documentation":"Shows/hides a named object from a Cutscener in the scene \u2014 e.g. <<enable ElderAmos>> / <<disable ElderAmos>>, matching whatever name was given to that entry in the Cutscener's Objects list.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":597,"character":4},"end":{"line":601,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"objectName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"disable","definitionName":"global::DialogueManager.Disable","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":603,"character":4},"end":{"line":607,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"objectName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"placeat","definitionName":"global::DialogueManager.PlaceAt","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","documentation":"<<placeat TrueHaze HazeThree>> \u2014 puts the first object exactly where the second one is, matching its facing, instantly. Made for swapping a cutscene stand-in for the real object: place, disable the stand-in, enable the real one, and the handover is invisible instead of the replacement popping in somewhere else.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":613,"character":4},"end":{"line":617,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"objectName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"},{"name":"referenceName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"face","definitionName":"global::DialogueManager.Face","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","documentation":"Forces a named object's facing outright, instead of whatever direction a <<movement>> happened to travel in. Two forms: <<face Josh left>>      \u2014 a fixed compass direction: left, right, up, down. <<face Josh HazeOne>>   \u2014 turn to look at ANOTHER registered object, wherever it currently is. Use the second form any time the player walked to the spot HIMSELF rather than being placed there by a <<movement>> \u2014 it is the only one that stays correct no matter which side he approached from. Both names must be registered in a Cutscener's Objects list (the same list <<enable>>/<<disable>> use); they may be in different Cutsceners.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":629,"character":4},"end":{"line":633,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"objectName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"},{"name":"towards","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"mist","definitionName":"global::DialogueManager.Mist","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","documentation":"Advances the story mist to stage N \u2014 e.g. <<mist 2>>. Stages only ever go up (calling a lower number than already reached is a no-op); see MistDirector for what each stage actually looks like.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":638,"character":4},"end":{"line":642,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"stage","isParamsArray":false,"type":"number"}]},{"yarnName":"add_objective","definitionName":"global::ObjectiveManager.AddObjectiveCommand","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\Objective Manager.cs","documentation":"Yarn Command to add objective","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":338,"character":4},"end":{"line":350,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"objectiveName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"open_quest_log","definitionName":"global::ObjectiveManager.OpenQuestLogCommand","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\Objective Manager.cs","documentation":"Yarn Command to open quest log","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":381,"character":4},"end":{"line":386,"character":5}},"parameters":[]},{"yarnName":"close_quest_log","definitionName":"global::ObjectiveManager.CloseQuestLogCommand","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\Objective Manager.cs","documentation":"Yarn Command to close quest log","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":389,"character":4},"end":{"line":394,"character":5}},"parameters":[]},{"yarnName":"follow","definitionName":"global::NpcFollow.StartFollowing","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\NPC\\NpcFollow.cs","documentation":"Yarn: <<follow Marcus>> \u2014 ele volta a seguir de onde estiver.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":152,"character":4},"end":{"line":153,"character":77}},"parameters":[{"name":"who","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"unfollow","definitionName":"global::NpcFollow.StopFollowing","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\NPC\\NpcFollow.cs","documentation":"Yarn: <<unfollow Marcus>> \u2014 ele para e fica onde esta, ate mandarem de novo.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":156,"character":4},"end":{"line":157,"character":77}},"parameters":[{"name":"who","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"formation","definitionName":"global::NpcFormation.Trigger","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\NPC\\NpcFormation.cs","documentation":"<<formation FriendsAtEldersHouse>> \u2014 static so the Yarn command needs no reference to a specific marker, matching how <<movement>> and <<enable>> already work.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":163,"character":4},"end":{"line":188,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"formationName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"walkto","definitionName":"global::NpcWalkTo.WalkTo","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\NPC\\NpcWalkTo.cs","documentation":"Yarn: <<walkto Marcus MarcusSpot>> \u2014 NAO bloqueia, o jogo segue enquanto ele anda.","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":200,"character":4},"end":{"line":220,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"who","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"},{"name":"markName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"playmusic","definitionName":"global::MusicManager.PlayMusicCommand","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\RPG Ports\\MusicManager.cs","documentation":"<summary> Yarn: <<playmusic \"trackName\">> Plays a track from the musicTracks list by name. </summary>","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":98,"character":4},"end":{"line":116,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"musicName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"stopmusic","definitionName":"global::MusicManager.StopMusicCommand","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\RPG Ports\\MusicManager.cs","documentation":"<summary> Yarn: <<stopmusic>> Stops whatever is currently playing. </summary>","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":135,"character":4},"end":{"line":140,"character":5}},"parameters":[]},{"yarnName":"hint","definitionName":"global::TutorialHint.Hint","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\TutorialHint.cs","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":190,"character":4},"end":{"line":191,"character":60}},"parameters":[{"name":"texto","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}]},{"yarnName":"hintoff","definitionName":"global::TutorialHint.HintOff","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\TutorialHint.cs","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":193,"character":4},"end":{"line":194,"character":47}},"parameters":[]},{"yarnName":"ghosttutorial","definitionName":"global::TutorialHint.GhostTutorial","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\TutorialHint.cs","documentation":"<<ghosttutorial>> \u2014 PARA o dialogo e conduz o jogador pela mecanica inteira.  A sequencia toda mora aqui, e nao espalhada em gatilhos da cena, porque ela e uma coisa so: tutorial tem ORDEM, e ordem quebrada em cinco objetos diferentes fica impossivel de ler depois. Cada passo espera um FATO do jogo, nunca um tempo fixo:  1. \"aperte Q\"                  -> espera ele de fato assumir a Haze 2. \"aperte E na estatua\"       -> espera QUALQUER estatua girar 3. camera e controle voltam ao Josh na hora, faixa some 4. RETORNA: o resto da conversa roda, com a camera nele 5. conversa acabou -> devolve a Haze e ensina o Q de volta  O passo 5 nao cabe aqui dentro: enquanto este comando nao retornar, a conversa nao anda, e ele so faz sentido DEPOIS dela. Por isso sai numa corrotina solta.  O E flutuante da estatua fica suprimido do passo 1 ao 5 inteiro \u2014 so volta quando o jogador aperta o Q final. Durante o tutorial a instrucao ja esta na faixa, e o mesmo pedido em dois lugares divide a atencao de quem ainda nao sabe onde olhar.","language":"csharp","async":true,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":249,"character":4},"end":{"line":334,"character":5}},"parameters":[]}],"functions":[{"yarnName":"hasprogress","definitionName":"global::DialogueManager.HasProgress","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\ImageScript.cs","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":369,"character":4},"end":{"line":377,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"progressID","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}],"return":{"type":"bool"}},{"yarnName":"objective_completed","definitionName":"global::ObjectiveManager.ObjectiveCompleted","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\Objective Manager.cs","documentation":"Yarn Command to check if objective is completed","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":353,"character":4},"end":{"line":364,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"objectiveName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}],"return":{"type":"bool"}},{"yarnName":"objective_active","definitionName":"global::ObjectiveManager.ObjectiveActive","fileName":"ecdd adventure game\\Assets\\Scripts\\Dialogue Scripts\\Objective Manager.cs","documentation":"Yarn Command to check if objective is active","language":"csharp","async":false,"containsErrors":false,"location":{"start":{"line":367,"character":4},"end":{"line":378,"character":5}},"parameters":[{"name":"objectiveName","isParamsArray":false,"type":"string"}],"return":{"type":"bool"}}]}